<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Golden Ass</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Metamorphoses of Apuleius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Golden Ass, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> title is Metamorphoses, is a novel by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apuleius">Apuleius</a> written in the 2nd century CE in Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. It tells how Lucius, turned into a donkey by a magic mishap, passes through many adventures before being restored by the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isis">Isis</a>. It is the only ancient Latin novel to survive complete and contains the tale of Cupid and Psyche.</p></div>
